<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e338713da62> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1712] Apple’s test vehicles, which are modified Lexus SUVs, struggled to navigate streets near its Silicon Valley headquarters without the maps, smacking into curbs and sometimes having trouble staying in their lanes while crossing intersections, according to two people who worked on the program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/250dffe0af36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Inside Apple’s Eight-Year Struggle to Build a Self-Driving Car" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e091493d860> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple is entering a crowded field where rivals such as Alphabet Inc's Waymo unit and traditional carmakers such as General Motors Co's Cruise Automation, as well as start-ups such as Silicon Valley's Zoox, are pouring billions of dollars into cars that can drive themselves." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42159d83bd8e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "putting it in direct competition with most of Tesla's range and other luxury companies like Lucid." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ce4849c2a04> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Apple Car's First Test Drive Was A Total Disaster" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/604c55541c64> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On August 24, 1 of Apple's Lexus RX 450h self-driving test vehicles in \"autonomous mode\" was merging south on the Lawrence Expressway" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/66801b3678dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Based on reports automakers have made with U.S. safety regulators, Tesla vehicles were involved in 273 of the close to 400 accidents caused by autonomous driving technology over an 11-month period." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6db93a4e2752> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple’s self-driving cars ‘smacked into curbs, veered out of lanes’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74bfa3144682> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The demonstration was even filmed using aerial drones. The images and footage were then used to make a flashy promotional video to impress top Apple executives, including CEO Tim Cook, according to the report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8130ce2d4d78> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While Tesla, Mercedes, and BMW all aim to add self-driving features to what you may recognize as a standard road car, Apple's proposed product may not be what you expect a vehicle to look like." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/82e62de29ab4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1103] On August 24, 1 of Apple's Lexus RX 450h self-driving test vehicles in \"autonomous mode\" was merging south on the Lawrence Expressway in Sunnyvale, California at less than 1.6kph when it was rear-ended by a 2016 Nissan Leaf going about 24kph, according to the report posted on the California Department of Motor Vehicles website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/965a68fb026d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "If rumors are to be believed, Apple's fully-autonomous self-driving car will not feature any windows." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a2ce6b30c624> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple's car was first rumored back in 2015 with the launch of Project Titan." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c39adc34deda> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla, the leading electric car maker whose vehicles include semi-autonomous technology such as autopilot, \"full self-driving,\" and traffic-aware cruise control features, is under investigation by the federal government after drivers got into more than 200 crashes using assistance software" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4c74ad33c6c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1712] Apple’s test vehicles, which are modified Lexus SUVs, struggled to navigate streets near its Silicon Valley headquarters without the maps, smacking into curbs and sometimes having trouble staying in their lanes while crossing intersections, according to two people who worked on the program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9813c757495> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple Lexus RX 450h self-driving test car rear-ended during road testing in Silicon Valley" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce8dc975e010> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1712] Apple’s test vehicles, which are modified Lexus SUVs, struggled to navigate streets near its Silicon Valley headquarters without the maps, smacking into curbs and sometimes having trouble staying in their lanes while crossing intersections, according to two people who worked on the program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d954ab2e8549> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "some of the mishaps occurred while Tesla's Full Self-Driving mode was active." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d9f01b0a30b4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company has filed a patent for a \"VR system for use in autonomous vehicles with no windows,\" and it's easy to speculate where the technology for that patent may end up." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e1f6af155926> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple has been trying to work out the kinks in Project Titan, its autonomous electric vehicle program" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ebbe35688dbc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Now news has emerged about the autonomous car's driving abilities. If true, far from being road-ready, Apple's driving AI might actually be a bit dangerous in its present iteration." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

