<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/092dbbbeb929> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1711] Apple’s self-driving cars had trouble navigating streets, frequently bumped into curbs and veered out of lanes in the middle of intersections during test drives near the company’s Silicon Valley headquarters, according to a report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cfd98c0fd7c8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1103] On August 24, 1 of Apple's Lexus RX 450h self-driving test vehicles in \"autonomous mode\" was merging south on the Lawrence Expressway in Sunnyvale, California at less than 1.6kph when it was rear-ended by a 2016 Nissan Leaf going about 24kph, according to the report posted on the California Department of Motor Vehicles website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e78ae2830dca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1103] On August 24, 1 of Apple's Lexus RX 450h self-driving test vehicles in \"autonomous mode\" was merging south on the Lawrence Expressway in Sunnyvale, California at less than 1.6kph when it was rear-ended by a 2016 Nissan Leaf going about 24kph, according to the report posted on the California Department of Motor Vehicles website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/024167bd897c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Ian Goodfellow, a renowned scientist who headed the machine-learning division within Project Titan, left the company, the report stated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c6b986ac9a8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The data included crashes that happened while drivers were using features like Traffic Aware Cruise Control, but some of the mishaps occurred while Tesla's Full Self-Driving mode was active." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a6a057abcd4f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Head self-driving engineer Joe Bass left for Meta, while Doug Field — who was also working on the project — decided to jump ship and join Ford." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1713" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5bb8f91321b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Aerial drones filmed the drive, from Bozeman to the ski resort town of Big Sky, so that Apple managers could produce a polished film, with picturesque mountains in the background, to show CEO Tim Cook how their costly and long-running autonomous car project, Titan, was making progress." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ec9a458aa7a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The safety of self-driving cars has become a source of concern for US transportation regulators this year after one of Uber Technologies Inc's vehicles struck and killed a woman in March in Arizona, prompting the company to shut down its testing efforts for a time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a0691fcb592e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, which oversees motor vehicle transportation safety, would not say whether the drivers involved were using any of the semi-autonomous features when the crash occurred along I-95 near Gainesville." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd7c944eb648> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple’s test vehicles, which are modified Lexus SUVs, struggled to navigate streets near its Silicon Valley headquarters without the maps, smacking into curbs and sometimes having trouble staying in their lanes while crossing intersections, according to two people who worked on the program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1712" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c5f9a4dc050> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple has been trying to work out the kinks in Project Titan, its autonomous electric vehicle program, since it sent several of the self-driving cars on a test run along a 40-mile stretch from Bozeman, Mont., to the nearby Big Sky ski resort last August, according to The Information." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8b77e5ac9ba2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On August 24, 1 of Apple's Lexus RX 450h self-driving test vehicles in \"autonomous mode\" was merging south on the Lawrence Expressway in Sunnyvale, California at less than 1.6kph when it was rear-ended by a 2016 Nissan Leaf going about 24kph, according to the report posted on the California Department of Motor Vehicles website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/529542f4d073> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An Apple Inc self-driving car was rear-ended while merging onto an expressway near the company's Silicon Valley headquarters this month, the company said in an accident report posted on Friday (local time) that confirmed the iPhone maker is still in the race to build autonomous vehicles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1103" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7910e1504b40> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla, the leading electric car maker whose vehicles include semi-autonomous technology such as autopilot, “full self-driving,” and traffic-aware cruise control features, is under investigation by the federal government after drivers got into more than 200 crashes using assistance software." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ead26ab7a4f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Apple’s self-driving cars had trouble navigating streets, frequently bumped into curbs and veered out of lanes in the middle of intersections during test drives near the company’s Silicon Valley headquarters, according to a report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1711" .

